terms.medium_def:
A man from the tribe of Benjamin living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.8.10; 
only referred to as Sachia (שָֽׂכְיָה); 
son of Shaharaim and Hodesh; 
a brother of Jobab, Zibia, Mesha, Malcam, Jeuz, Mirmah, Abitub and Elpaal. § a Benjamite, son of Shaharaim by his wife Hodesh

A man from the tribe of Naphtali living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at Gen.46.24; 
referred to as Jezer (יֵ֫צֶר), or Jezerite (יִצְרִי); 
son of Naphtali; 
a brother of Jahzeel, Guni and Shillem. § the 3rd son of Naphtali and the founder of the family of Jezerites

A man from the tribe of Levi living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Ch.25.3; 
referred to as Zeri (צְרִי), or Izri (יִצְרִי); 
son of Jeduthun; 
a brother of Obed-edom, Mattithiah, Gedaliah, Jeshaiah and Hashabiah. § a leader of one of the Levitical sanctuary choirs

A man from the tribe of Naphtali living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at Gen.46.24; 
referred to as Jezer (יֵ֫צֶר), or Jezerite (יִצְרִי); 
son of Naphtali; 
a brother of Jahzeel, Guni and Shillem. § descendants of Jezer the son of Naphtali

A man of the Arabs living at the time of the Patriarchs, first mentioned at Gen.25.15; 
only referred to as Naphish (נָפִישׁ); 
son of Ishmael; 
a brother of Nebaioth, Kedar, Adbeel, Mibsam, Mishma, Dumah, Massa, Hadad, Tema, Jetur, Kedemah and Mahalath.

People from Naphtuh(?) of the Egyptians, first mentioned at Gen.10.13; 
only referred to as Naphtuhim (נַפְתֻּחִים); 
descended from Egypt along with Ludim, Anamim, Lehabim, Pathrusim, Casluhim and Caphtorim. § an unclear reference to Egypt; perhaps Lower Egypt

A man living at the time before the Flood, first mentioned at Gen.5.12; 
referred to as Mahalalel (מַהֲלַלְאֵל), or Mahalaleel (NIV= Mahalel) (Μαλελεήλ); 
a son of Kenan; 
father of Jared.

A man living before Israel's Monarchy, first mentioned at Jdg.12.13; 
only referred to as Hillel (הִלֵּל); 
father of Abdon. § a native of Pirathon in Mount Ephraim, the father of Abdon the judge

A man from the tribe of Judah living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.4.16; 
only referred to as Jehallelel (יְהַלֶּלְאֵל); 
father of Ziph, Ziphah, Tiria, Asarel.

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 2Ch.29.12; 
only referred to as Jehallelel (יְהַלֶּלְאֵל); 
father of Azariah.

A man living at the time of Exile and Return, only mentioned at Neh.11.4; 
only referred to as Mahalalel (מַהֲלַלְאֵל); 
father of Shephatiah.

A king of Northern Israel, living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 2Ki.15.14; 
only referred to as Menahem (מְנַחֵם); 
a son of Gadi; 
father of Pekahiah. § son of Gadi and king of the northern kingdom of Israel; slew the usurper Shallum to ascend the throne and reigned for ten years; contemporary with prophets Hosea and Amos

A man living at the time of Exile and Return, first mentioned at Neh.1.1; 
only referred to as Nehemiah (נְחֶמְיָה); 
son of Hacaliah; 
a brother of Hanani.

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 2Ki.25.23; 
only referred to as Tanhumeth (תַּנְחֻ֫מֶת); 
father of Seraiah. § father of Seraiah, a leader who joined Gedaliah after Jerusalem's fall

A man from the tribe of Judah(?) living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.4.19; 
only referred to as Naham (נַ֫חַם); 
a brother of Hodiah. § the brother of IIodiah or Jehudijah, wife of Ezra

A man living at the time of Exile and Return, only mentioned at Neh.3.16; 
only referred to as Nehemiah (נְחֶמְיָה); 
a son of Azbuk.

A man from the tribe of Levi living at the time of Exile and Return, first mentioned at 1Ch.9.14; 
only referred to as Hashabiah (חֲשַׁבְיָ֫הוּ); 
a son of Bunni; 
father of Azrikam.

A man from the tribe of Levi living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Ch.25.3; 
only referred to as Hashabiah (חֲשַׁבְיָ֫הוּ); 
son of Jeduthun; 
a brother of Obed-edom, Mattithiah, Gedaliah, Zeri, Jeshaiah.

A man from the tribe of Levi living at the time of Exile and Return, first mentioned at 1Ch.9.14; 
only referred to as Hasshub (חַשּׁוּב); 
a son of Azrikam; 
father of Shemaiah.

A man from the tribe of Judah living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.3.20; 
only referred to as Hashubah (חֲשֻׁבָה); 
son of Zerubbabel; 
a brother of Meshullam, Hananiah, Shelomith, Ohel, Berechiah, Hasadiah, Jushab-hesed, Abiud. § a son of Zerubbabel

A man from the tribe of Levi living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.6.45; 
only referred to as Hashabiah (חֲשַׁבְיָ֫הוּ); 
a son of Amaziah; 
father of Malluch.

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.27.17; 
only referred to as Hashabiah (חֲשַׁבְיָ֫הוּ); 
a son of Kemuel.

A man living at the time of Exile and Return, only mentioned at Neh.11.22; 
only referred to as Hashabiah (חֲשַׁבְיָ֫הוּ); 
son of Mattaniah; 
a brother of Shemaiah; 
father of Bani.

A man living at the time of Exile and Return, only mentioned at Neh.3.10; 
only referred to as Hashabneiah (חֲשַׁבְנְיָה); 
father of Hattush.

A man living at the time of Exile and Return, only mentioned at Neh.3.11; 
only referred to as Hasshub (חַשּׁוּב); 
a son of Pahath-moab.

to credit, count, reckon; regard, think, consider 
(1) primarily to count, calculate; to count, enumerate, consider Mk. 15:28; Lk. 22:37; to set down as a matter of account, 1Cor. 13:5; 2Cor. 3:5; 12:6; to impute, credit, count, consider, reckon Rom. 4:3; 2Cor. 5:19; 2Tim. 4:16; to account, Rom. 2:26; 8:36; εἰς οὐδὲν λογισθῆναι, to be set at nought, despised, Acts 19:27; to regard, deem, consider, Rom. 6:11; 14:14; 1Cor. 4:1; 2Cor. 10:2; Phil. 3:13; 
(2) to infer, conclude, presume, Rom. 2:3; 3:28; 8:18; 2Cor. 10:2, 7, 11; Heb. 11:19; 1Pet. 5:12; 
(3) to think upon, ponder, Phil. 4:8; absolute to reason, Mk. 11:31; 1Cor. 13:11

A location first mentioned at 1Ki.13.32; 
referred to as Samaria (שֹׁמְרוֹן), or Samaria (Aramiac שׇֽׁמְרָ֑יִן), or Samaritan (שֹׁמרֹנִי), or Samaria (Σαμάρεια), or Samaritan (Σαμαρείτης), or Samaria (NIV= Samaritan) or Samaritan (Σαμαρεῖτις). § ♣1) the region of northern Palestine associated with the northern kingdom of the 10 tribes of Israel which split from the kingdom after the death of Solomon during the reign of his son Rehoboam and were ruled by Jeroboam
2) the capital city of the northern kingdom of Israel located 30 miles (50 km) north of Jerusalem and 6 miles (10 km) northwest of Shechem

A man from the tribe of Issachar living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at Gen.46.13; 
referred to as Shimron (שִׁמְרוֹן), or Shimronite (שִׁמְרֹנִי); 
son of Issachar; 
a brother of Tola, Puah and Jashub. § 4th son of Issachar and the progenitor of the family of Shimronites

A man from the tribe of Benjamin living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.8.18; 
only referred to as Ishmerai (יִשְׁמְרַי); 
son of Elpaal; 
a brother of Eber, Misham, Shemed, Beriah, Shema, Zebadiah, Meshullam, Hizki, Heber, Izliah and Jobab. § a Benjamite of the family of Elpaal

A man of the Moabites living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 2Ki.12.21; 
referred to as Shomer (שֹׁמֵר), or Shimrith (שִׁמְרִית); 
father of Jehozabad.

A man from the tribe of Asher living before Israel's Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Ch.7.32; 
referred to as Shomer (שֹׁמֵר), or Shemer (KJV= Shamer, NIV= Shomer) (שֶׁ֫מֶר); 
son of Heber; 
a brother of Japhlet, Hotham and Shua; 
father of Ahi, Rohgah, Jehubbah and Aram.

A man from the tribe of Benjamin living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.8.12; 
only referred to as Shemed (שָׁ֫מֶד); 
son of Elpaal; 
a brother of Eber, Misham, Beriah, Shema, Zebadiah, Meshullam, Hizki, Heber, Ishmerai, Izliah and Jobab. §a Benjamite, son of Elpaal and builder of the towns of Ono and Lod

A man from the tribe of Levi living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.6.46; 
only referred to as Shemer (שֶׁ֫מֶר); 
a son of Mahli; 
father of Bani. §a Benjamite, son of Elpaal and builder of the towns of Ono and Lod

A man from the tribe of Asher living before Israel's Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Ch.7.32; 
referred to as Shomer (שֹׁמֵר), or Shemer (KJV= Shamer, NIV= Shomer) (שֶׁ֫מֶר); 
son of Heber; 
a brother of Japhlet, Hotham and Shua; 
father of Ahi, Rohgah, Jehubbah and Aram. §a Benjamite, son of Elpaal and builder of the towns of Ono and Lod

A man from the tribe of Simeon(?) living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.4.37; 
only referred to as Shimri (שִׁמְרִי); 
a son of Shemaiah; 
father of Jedaiah.

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.11.45; 
only referred to as Shimri (שִׁמְרִי); 
father of Jediael, Joha.

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.26.10; 
only referred to as Shimri (שִׁמְרִי); 
son of Hosah; 
a brother of Hilkiah, Tebaliah and Zechariah.

A man from the tribe of Judah living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 2Ch.11.19; 
only referred to as Shemariah (שְׁמַרְיָ֫הוּ); 
son of Rehoboam and Mahalath; 
a brother of Jeush and Zaham; 
half-brother of: Abijah, Attai, Ziza and Shelomith.

A man of the Moabites living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 2Ki.12.21; 
referred to as Shomer (שֹׁמֵר), or Shimrith (שִׁמְרִית); 
father of Jehozabad. § a Moabitess, mother of Jehozabad, one of the assassins of king Joash of Judah

A man from the tribe of Issachar living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at Gen.46.13; 
referred to as Shimron (שִׁמְרוֹן), or Shimronite (שִׁמְרֹנִי); 
son of Issachar; 
a brother of Tola, Puah and Jashub. § Shimronites, of Shimron "guardian"
descendants of Shimron

A man from the tribe of Benjamin living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.8.21; 
only referred to as Shimrath (שִׁמְרָת); 
son of Shimei; 
a brother of Jakim, Zichri, Zabdi, Elienai, Zillethai, Eliel, Adaiah and Beraiah. § a Benjamite, son of Shimei

A Singer from the tribe of Levi living at the time of Exile and Return, first mentioned at 1Ch.9.21; 
only referred to as Zechariah (זְכַרְיָהוּ); 
son of Meshelemiah; 
a brother of Jediael, Zebadiah, Jathniel, Elam, Jehohanan and Eliehoenai.

A man from the tribe of Levi living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Ch.25.2; 
only referred to as Zaccur (זַכּוּר); 
son of Asaph; 
a brother of Joseph, Nethaniah and Asharelah.

A king of Northern Israel, living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 2Ki.14.29; 
only referred to as Zechariah (זְכַרְיָהוּ); 
a son of Jeroboam. § 11th in order of the minor prophets; a priest, son of Berechiah and grandson of Iddo, who, along with Haggai, directed the rebuilding of the temple in the days of Zerubbabel

A prophet living at the time of Exile and Return, first mentioned at Ezr.5.1; 
referred to as Zechariah (זְכַרְיָהוּ), or Zechariah (Aramiac זְכַרְיָה); 
a son of Berechiah. § 11th in order of the minor prophets; a priest, son of Berechiah and grandson of Iddo, who, along with Haggai, directed the rebuilding of the temple in the days of Zerubbabel

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 2Ki.18.2; 
only referred to as Zechariah (זְכַרְיָהוּ); 
father of Abi. § 11th in order of the minor prophets; a priest, son of Berechiah and grandson of Iddo, who, along with Haggai, directed the rebuilding of the temple in the days of Zerubbabel

A man living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, only mentioned at Num.13.4; 
only referred to as Zaccur (זַכּוּר); 
father of Shammua.

A man from the tribe of Simeon living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.4.26; 
only referred to as Zaccur (זַכּוּר); 
a son of Hammuel; 
father of Shimei.

A man from the tribe of Levi living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.24.27; 
only referred to as Zaccur (זַכּוּר); 
son of Jaaziah; 
a brother of Beno, Shoham and Ibri.

A man living at the time of Exile and Return, only mentioned at Neh.3.2; 
only referred to as Zaccur (זַכּוּר); 
a son of Imri.

A priest living at the time of Exile and Return, only mentioned at Neh.13.13; 
only referred to as Zaccur (זַכּוּר); 
a son of Mattaniah; 
father of Hanan.

A man from the tribe of Benjamin living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Ch.8.31; 
referred to as Zecher (זֶ֫כֶר), or Zechariah (זְכַרְיָהוּ); 
son of Abiel and Maacah; 
a brother of Kish, Ner, Abdon, Zur, Baal, Nadab, Gedor, Ahio and Mikloth. § a Gibeonite

A man from the tribe of Levi living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, only mentioned at Exo.6.21; 
only referred to as Zichri (זִכְרִי); 
son of Izhar; 
a brother of Korah, Nepheg and Shelomith.

A man from the tribe of Benjamin living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.8.19; 
only referred to as Zichri (זִכְרִי); 
son of Shimei; 
a brother of Jakim, Zabdi, Elienai, Zillethai, Eliel, Adaiah, Beraiah and Shimrath.

A man from the tribe of Benjamin living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.8.23; 
only referred to as Zichri (זִכְרִי); 
son of Shashak; 
a brother of Ishpan, Eber, Eliel, Abdon, Hanan, Hananiah, Elam, Anthothijah, Iphdeiah and Penuel.

A man from the tribe of Benjamin living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.8.27; 
only referred to as Zichri (זִכְרִי); 
son of Jeroham; 
a brother of Shamsherai, Shehariah, Athaliah, Jaareshiah and Elijah.

A man from the tribe of Levi living at the time of Exile and Return, first mentioned at 1Ch.9.15; 
referred to as Zichri (זִכְרִי), or Zabdi (זַבְדִּי); 
a son of Asaph; 
father of Mica.

A man from the tribe of Levi living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.26.25; 
only referred to as Zichri (זִכְרִי); 
a son of Joram; 
father of Shelomoth.

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.27.16; 
only referred to as Zichri (זִכְרִי); 
father of Eliezer.

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 2Ch.17.16; 
only referred to as Zichri (זִכְרִי); 
father of Amasiah.

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 2Ch.23.1; 
only referred to as Zichri (זִכְרִי); 
father of Elishaphat.

A man living at the time of Exile and Return, only mentioned at Neh.11.9; 
